Falsifies `paging::sv39::verification::a_block_keeps_address_and_permissions_apart`.

The defect: `Sv39::block_entry` hands `pa` to `leaf_entry` without masking it to the
superpage's alignment, on the reasoning that Sv39 superpages are "the same leaf at a
higher level" (which is true of the permission bits and not of the PPN). A megapage
whose PPN has any of its low 9 bits set, or a gigapage with any of its low 18, is a
misaligned superpage, and the hardware raises a page fault on it rather than ignoring
the bits.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(ppn_as_address, pa & pa_bits, ...)` for any `pa` with a
bit set below the superpage's alignment.

diff --git a/crates/paging/src/sv39.rs b/crates/paging/src/sv39.rs
index 2c4e4062..f3b03f86 100644
--- a/crates/paging/src/sv39.rs
+++ b/crates/paging/src/sv39.rs
@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@ impl PageFormat for Sv39 {
     /// the PPN: its low 9 (megapage) or 18 (gigapage) bits must be zero, or the hardware raises a
     /// misaligned-superpage page fault, so the address is masked to the block's alignment.
     fn block_entry(pa: u64, flags: Flags, size: PageSize) -> Option<u64> {
-        Some(Self::leaf_entry(pa & !(size.bytes() - 1), flags))
+        Some(Self::leaf_entry(pa, flags))
     }
 
     /// R, W or X set: a leaf, at whatever level. All three clear: a pointer.
